# Redirects for whysheet.press.
#
# Kept deliberately short. Netlify's Pretty URLs already serve /about/ and
# /packet/ from their index.html, so rules for those would be dead weight.

# The shapes people will guess, because stimpunks.org spells it /why/ and every
# sheet's own licence block names a GitHub file. Somebody typing a slug they saw
# on paper should land on the sheet, not on a 404.
/why/*           /sheets/:splat    301
/sheet/*         /sheets/:splat    301
/broadside/*     /broadsides/:splat 301

# The packet has been called a few things in drafts; keep them all working.
/build           /packet/          301
/packets/*       /packet/          301

# The mirrored WordPress blocks in broadsides/source/ are source, not pages: each
# is a bare fragment carrying an inline <style> and an inline <script>, which our
# Content-Security-Policy blocks. A reader who found one would get it unstyled and
# inert. They stay in the repository — readable on GitHub, which is where source
# belongs — and anyone who asks for one here gets the broadside itself.
#
# The `!` is load-bearing. Netlify serves an existing static file BEFORE applying
# a redirect, so without it this rule never fires — verified on the live deploy,
# where /broadsides/source/eye-contact.block.html returned 200 and the raw
# fragment. The shadowing form forces the redirect even though the file is there.
/broadsides/source/*   /broadsides/   301!

# The press has one address. Netlify keeps serving the project's own
# why-sheet-press.netlify.app hostname at 200 alongside the custom domain, with
# byte-identical content — verified, the two responses hash the same. That is a
# second address for a site whose whole point is a memorable URL printed on
# paper, and it is the hostname that carries Netlify's platform HSTS with
# `preload`, which `_headers` deliberately does not set.
#
# Star Stuff and Queering Earth already redirect theirs; Penguin Pebbling does
# not. This matches the better-configured half, and lives here rather than in a
# dashboard setting so it is reviewable in a diff like everything else.
https://why-sheet-press.netlify.app/*   https://whysheet.press/:splat   301!
